        "geology": "Mountains built by crystalline core (granit) surrounded by Paleogenne sedimets in valleys. In mountains and foothills dominate: Quatternary sediments - (glacial) moraines, glacifluvial and fluvila sediments",
        "hydrology": "Steep precipitation gradient, from 800 mm/year in lower part up to 1800 mm/year in the upper part of the site. Maximum precipitation ammount in summer. Typical characteristic is low evaporation causing high runoff from the mountains. In winter water accumulated in snow (November-May). High stoniness on morains is reason for low water table. Rivers are generally small and network dense.",
        "soils": "Lithosols in the highest part Rankers in apline meadows and sublpine ecosystems, partly in forest Podsols and Cabisols dominates in spruce forest Pseudogleys in the lower part, alluvial forest",
        "vegetation": "Larche-spruce oligotrophic forest dominates. In 2004 forest was heavily affected by windstorm. Due to windfall and consequent bark beetle attack only 25% of previous forest has remained standing."
